course: dictionary
lesson: 11772
title: Everyday words: bathtub
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bathtub is a large container for water that you sit or lie in to wash your body. Another name for it is a bath. The words around it give you clues about what it is for.
explain: «Mum filled the bathtub with warm water.» Filled tells you that water goes inside, and warm water tells you it is for washing. Try swapping in the word bath: the sentence still makes sense, so the two words mean the same thing.
explain: Some sentences teach you safety. «Never leave a small child alone in a bathtub.» Never means at no time at all, so this is a rule to keep children safe.
explain: In maths, a bathtub often appears in problems about filling or emptying. If a tap fills it at a steady number of litres per minute, multiply the litres per minute by the number of minutes to find the total litres.
fact: Bathtub is a noun. Its plural is bathtubs.
fact: «Bathtub» means a large container for water that you sit or lie in to wash your body.
fact: A bathtub is another word for a bath.
fact: Useful phrases: fill the bathtub, and in the bathtub. «Sam sat in the bathtub and sang.»
fact: Never leave a small child alone in a bathtub, even for a moment.
exercise: «Mum filled the bathtub with warm water.» What is a bathtub? | A towel for drying your hair | A large container for water that you sit or lie in to wash | *A large container for water that you sit or lie in to wash your body | A room with a toilet and a sink
exercise: Why must you never leave a small child alone in a bathtub? | *Because they could get hurt or drown in the water | Because the bathtub needs cleaning | Because the water must be changed | Because the room gets cold
exercise: «The tap fills the bathtub at 10 litres per minute.» If the tap runs for 5 minutes, how many litres go in? | *50 litres | 500 litres | 2 litres | 15 litres
test: «Sam lay in the bathtub and washed his hair.» Where was Sam? | In the kitchen | On the stairs | In the garden | *In the bathtub
test: Which word means the same as bathtub? | Bathmat | Bathroom | *Bath | Bathrobe
exam: Tap A fills a bathtub at 8 litres per minute. How many litres go in after 4 minutes? | *32 litres | 24 litres | 12 litres | 40 litres
